@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- ca-interpretation-nouns.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: the nouns that the pass-2 modules share.
-- Nouns only: DECLARE and nothing else.  No rule, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT.  The pass-1 modules keep their own nouns (the time module's
-- `A moment`, the calendar module's `A standard time`); the pass-2 modules (definitions, reading, powers) import this one so that
-- two of them never invent a different type for the same thing.
-- Every constructor is a fact a witness could state: "it is a regulation", "it is a marginal note", "it is in Ontario".  Whether the
-- Act makes anything of it is the business of the module that uses it.

§ `Kinds of instrument (sections 2(1) and 35(1))`

-- "Act" is an Act of Parliament (s 2(1)); an Act of a legislature is another thing (s 35(1) "Act" speaks of it); an enactment is an Act
-- or regulation or any portion of either (s 2(1)).
DECLARE `A kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of Parliament`
    `an Act of a legislature`
    `a regulation`
    `a portion of an Act of Parliament`
    `a portion of a regulation`
    `an instrument of none of these kinds`

§ `Provinces and territories (sections 2(1), 35(1))`

-- The ten provinces and three territories that the Act names.  Used by "province", "territory", "lieutenant governor in council",
-- "superior court" and the other definitions that speak place by place.
DECLARE `A province or territory` IS ONE OF
    `Newfoundland and Labrador`
    `Prince Edward Island`
    `Nova Scotia`
    `New Brunswick`
    `Quebec`
    `Ontario`
    `Manitoba`
    `Saskatchewan`
    `Alberta`
    `British Columbia`
    `Yukon`
    `the Northwest Territories`
    `Nunavut`

§ `Parts of an enactment as printed (sections 13 and 14)`

-- What the Act says something about in sections 13 and 14: the preamble, a marginal note, and a reference to a former enactment that
-- appears after the end of a section or other division; anything else in the printed text is `another part of the printed text`.
DECLARE `A part of an enactment as printed` IS ONE OF
    `the preamble`
    `a marginal note`
    `a reference to a former enactment that appears after the end of a section or other division`
    `a reference to a former enactment that appears elsewhere in the printed text`
    `another part of the printed text`

§ `Kinds of division that a reference points at (section 41)`

DECLARE `A kind of division referred to` IS ONE OF
    `a part`
    `a division`
    `a section`
    `a schedule`
    `an appendix`
    `a form`
    `a subsection`
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `a clause`
    `a subclause`
    `regulations`
    `anything else`

§ `Words, and what they import (section 33)`

DECLARE `What a word imports` IS ONE OF
    `female persons`
    `male persons`
    `corporations`
    `something else`

DECLARE `A grammatical number` IS ONE OF
    `the singular`
    `the plural`

DECLARE `A form of a word` IS ONE OF
    `the word as defined`
    `another part of speech of the word defined`
    `another grammatical form of the word defined`
    `a different word`

§ `Ways of citing an enactment (section 40)`

DECLARE `A way of citing an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes`
    `by its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
    `by its long title`
    `by its short title`
    `by the Act under which it was made`
    `by the number or designation under which it was registered by the Clerk of the Privy Council`
    `by some other description`
